WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.514
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:08.096
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.396 --> 00:00:14.276
Unit twenty-one: Excellent Service. In this unit, you will make polite requests and ask indirect questions.

4
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:16.528
refund policy.

5
00:00:17.228 --> 00:00:21.178
refund policy means the shop's rules about giving money back.

6
00:00:21.478 --> 00:00:24.708
The refund policy allows returns within thirty days.

7
00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:28.003
Your turn. Say: refund policy.

8
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:31.971
refund policy.

9
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:34.089
polite request.

10
00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:38.321
polite request means asking for something in a kind, formal way.

11
00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:41.587
'Could you help me, please?' is a polite request.

12
00:00:42.287 --> 00:00:44.742
Your turn. Say: polite request.

13
00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:48.733
polite request.

14
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:50.660
helpdesk.

15
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.240
helpdesk means a place or service that helps customers with problems.

16
00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.120
Call the helpdesk if your internet stops working.

17
00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.973
Your turn. Say: helpdesk.

18
00:01:03.673 --> 00:01:04.674
helpdesk.

19
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:06.835
feedback form.

20
00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:10.858
feedback form means a form where customers give their opinions.

21
00:01:11.158 --> 00:01:13.634
Please complete the feedback form after your stay.

22
00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.615
Your turn. Say: feedback form.

23
00:01:19.315 --> 00:01:20.444
feedback form.

24
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.648
service quality.

25
00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:26.358
service quality means how good the service of a company is.

26
00:01:26.658 --> 00:01:29.064
The hotel is famous for its service quality.

27
00:01:29.764 --> 00:01:32.672
Your turn. Say: service quality.

28
00:01:35.372 --> 00:01:36.698
service quality.

29
00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:38.719
waiting time.

30
00:01:39.419 --> 00:01:41.581
waiting time means how long you have to wait.

31
00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:44.438
The waiting time at the bank was forty minutes.

32
00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.477
Your turn. Say: waiting time.

33
00:01:50.177 --> 00:01:51.306
waiting time.

34
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.469
solve a problem.

35
00:01:54.169 --> 00:01:56.981
solve a problem means to find an answer to a problem.

36
00:01:57.281 --> 00:01:59.733
The manager solved the problem in five minutes.

37
00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:03.202
Your turn. Say: solve a problem.

38
00:02:05.902 --> 00:02:06.972
solve a problem.

39
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:09.182
manager on duty.

40
00:02:09.882 --> 00:02:13.901
manager on duty means the manager who is working at that moment.

41
00:02:14.201 --> 00:02:16.456
I'd like to speak to the manager on duty.

42
00:02:17.156 --> 00:02:19.913
Your turn. Say: manager on duty.

43
00:02:22.613 --> 00:02:24.044
manager on duty.

44
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.073
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.373 --> 00:02:31.174
Excuse me. Could you tell me what the refund policy is?

46
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:35.995
Of course. You can return items within fourteen days.

47
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:40.154
Do you know whether I can get cash or only store credit?

48
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:44.381
I'm not sure. Let me ask the manager on duty.

49
00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:49.009
Thank you. Can you tell me how long the waiting time is?

50
00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:53.979
About five minutes. We'll solve the problem as quickly as we can.

51
00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:58.003
Grammar focus: Indirect questions.

52
00:02:58.303 --> 00:03:01.196
Indirect questions are more polite than direct questions.

53
00:03:01.496 --> 00:03:04.889
Start with could you tell me or do you know, then use normal word order.

54
00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:08.222
For example: Could you tell me where the helpdesk is?

55
00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:12.646
In indirect questions, use normal word order (subject + verb) and no do / does / did.

56
00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.569
Now read and listen. What Makes Great Service?.

57
00:03:16.869 --> 00:03:20.216
A recent survey asked customers what makes great service.

58
00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:24.898
Most people said that a short waiting time was the most important thing.

59
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:30.075
Many also wanted staff who could solve a problem without calling a manager.

60
00:03:31.383 --> 00:03:35.008
Polite requests and a friendly smile made customers feel respected.

61
00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:40.383
Companies that read every feedback form usually improve their service quality.

62
00:03:41.683 --> 00:03:44.103
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:44.403 --> 00:03:47.460
A service that helps customers with problems is a blank.

64
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.784
A, helpdesk. B, feedback form. C, refund policy.

65
00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:57.435
The answer is A: helpdesk.

66
00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.833
Could you tell me where the station blank?

67
00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.974
A, is. B, is it. C, does.

68
00:04:07.983 --> 00:04:09.321
The answer is A: is.

69
00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.234
Do you know blank the shop opens on Sunday?

70
00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.073
A, does. B, if. C, what.

71
00:04:20.083 --> 00:04:21.549
The answer is B: if.

72
00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.922
How long you have to wait is the blank.

73
00:04:25.222 --> 00:04:29.061
A, service quality. B, waiting time. C, polite request.

74
00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.119
The answer is B: waiting time.

75
00:04:36.617 --> 00:04:38.872
According to the survey, what was most important?

76
00:04:39.172 --> 00:04:43.847
A, a short waiting time. B, low prices. C, free gifts.

77
00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.198
The answer is A: a short waiting time.

78
00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:56.356
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe a time when you received excellent or poor service.

79
00:05:01.656 --> 00:05:07.231
At a phone shop, the staff solved my problem quickly and politely, so I wrote a great review.

80
00:05:07.531 --> 00:05:09.008
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:10.017 --> 00:05:14.074
Great work today! You learned eight new words and indirect questions.

82
00:05:14.374 --> 00:05:17.549
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

83
00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:20.466
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

84
00:05:20.766 --> 00:05:23.593
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

